To achieve this, the "Stop" item in the menu should trigger the following actions:

1. Retrieve the original broadcast intent from the `broadcastIntent` variable.
2. Call the `unregisterReceiver()` method to unregister the BroadcastReceiver associated with the LiveCard.
3. Use the `broadcastIntent` to send an `Intent` with action `android.content.Intent.ACTION_CANCEL` to cancel the ongoing notification.

Here's how you can implement the "Stop" item's click handler:

```java
@Override
public boolean onOptionsItemSelected(MenuItem item) {
    switch (item.getItemId()) {
        case R.id.host_card_stop:
            // Retrieve the original broadcast intent
            Intent stopIntent = broadcastIntent;

            // Unregister the BroadcastReceiver
            if (BroadcastReceiver.isRegistered(this, stopIntent.getAction())) {
                unregisterReceiver(new IntentFilter(stopIntent.getAction()));
            }

            // Cancel the notification
            sendBroadcast(stopIntent);

            // Inform the user that the LiveCard has been stopped
            Toast.makeText(this, "LiveCard stopped", Toast.LENGTH_SHORT).show();

            return true;
        default:
            return super.onOptionsItemSelected(item);
    }
}
