The movableRowsReceiver option should be set on the receiving table, and specifies the action that should be taken
when a row is dropped into it. 

The default value is "append", which means that the row will be appended to the table. 

Other possible values are:

- "prepend": The row will be prepended to the table.
- "replace": The row will replace the selected row in the table.
- "custom": A custom function can be provided to handle the row insertion.

Here is an example of how to set the movableRowsReceiver option:

```javascript
table.setOption("movableRowsReceiver", "append");
```

In the following example, a custom function is provided to handle the row insertion:

```javascript
function handleInsertion(row) {
    // Your custom logic here
    console.log("Row inserted:", row);
}

table.setOption("movableRowsReceiver", "custom", handleInsertion);
```

By using the movableRowsReceiver option, you can control how rows are inserted into the table when they are dragged and dropped.

